# What the backend lambda does NOT need.
#
# Vercel uploads the whole working directory unless told otherwise, and this
# repository is a monorepo whose other halves are enormous: the desktop client
# ships a PySide6 build environment and the web client a node_modules tree,
# together over 1.9 GB. Two copies of Qt6WebEngineCore.dll are individually
# larger than Vercel's 100 MB per-file limit, so with nothing ignored the
# deploy does not merely upload slowly -- it fails outright with
# "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)".
#
# The serverless function is api/index.py, which imports backend/app. That,
# plus requirements.txt, is the entire deployment.

# Virtualenvs -- the source of the >100 MB Qt DLLs.
.venv/
desktop/.venv-build/
**/venv/
**/.venv/

# The desktop client. Built and distributed through GitHub Releases by
# .github/workflows/desktop-release.yml, never through Vercel.
desktop/

# The web client. Deployed as its own Vercel project from frontend/.
frontend/

# Build and tooling noise.
node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.git/
.github/
scratch/
docs/
*.log

# Local databases and secrets. .env is gitignored, but a local file present in
# the working directory would otherwise still be uploaded.
*.db
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
